`var` is function-scoped, so there is one `i` shared by all three callbacks. The `setTimeout` callbacks run after the loop finishes, when `i` is 3, so each one logs 3.

Fix: use `let`, which creates a fresh binding per iteration:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```

Pre-ES6 alternative: wrap the body in an IIFE (`(function(j){ setTimeout(() => console.log(j), 0); })(i);`) to capture the value.
